{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>I am YHWH your Elohim, who brought you out of the land of Egypt to be unto you for an Elohim; I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> He explains here that the bringing out was so that He would be unto us for an Elohim; if so, the matter is not merely the need of an ordinary person, but rather the need of the Most High. And this is what Yehoshua said (Joshua 7:9): ״והכריתו את שמנו מן הארץ ומה תעשה לשמך הגדול״ — and what will You do for Your great Name — for if there is no people, the kingship of the King is not made known. And this verse began with 'I am YHWH your Elohim' and concluded with 'I am YHWH your Elohim' — that is, in this world and in the world to come." "<b>Or</b> it may say: 'I am YHWH your Elohim' — in the first redemption; that is what it says, 'who brought you out of the land of Egypt' — in the final redemption of the ingathering of exiles. And He promises us here the return of the Shekhinah in the ingathering of exiles, just as it was in the redemption from Egypt, which we do not find in the redemption of Babylonia, for the Shekhinah did not dwell in the Second Temple — and this is among the five things that were lacking there, as it is written (Haggai 1:8): ״וארצה בו ואכבדה״, and אכבד is written (defective, without a vav). And the verse equates the final redemption to the first redemption, and this is the word of the prophet (Isaiah 11:11): ״יוסיף ה׳ שנית ידו״, and it is written (Micah 7:15): ״כימי צאתך מארץ מצרים אראנו נפלאות״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "Source cites Joshua 7:9; the citation is written יהושע ז׳:ט׳ and the quotation matches Joshua 7:9, but the phrase is actually spoken by Joshua to HaShem, not by HaShem.", 1 "The opening '<b>או</b> יאמר' presents an alternative reading to the immediately preceding comment; the bold lemma marks only the word 'or.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:54.408086639Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}